    <string name="rules_title">How to play</string>
    <string name="rule_1_title">Moving</string>
    <string name="rule_1_body">Tap your piece, then a lit square. The last move is tinted. A king in check glows red.</string>
    <string name="rule_2_title">Castle, en passant, promotion</string>
    <string name="rule_2_body">Castle when the king and rook have not moved and the squares between them are empty. Capture en passant after a double pawn step. On the last rank, choose queen, rook, bishop or knight.</string>
    <string name="rule_3_title">Mate and draws</string>
    <string name="rule_3_body">Checkmate ends the game. No legal move without check is stalemate. Fifty moves, threefold repetition and insufficient material are draws.</string>
    <string name="rule_4_title">Hints and ads</string>
    <string name="rule_4_body">Each game starts with 3 hints. When they run out, a rewarded ad grants 3 more. An interstitial plays when a finished game returns to the menu or starts again. The bottom banner is a large banner, twice a standard banner tall.</string>
